{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide at least 512 MB of compressed in-memory swap on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"/dev/zram0 was active with a 536,870,912-byte capacity and zstd compression both before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9bf851a2208c4953","cmd-37a8c8cae3ab439c"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Ensure the compressed in-memory swap activates at boot.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The OpenRC local service was enabled, and a bounded reboot demonstrated that the zram swap automatically returned active with the same size and compression algorithm.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bec683a148c548da","cmd-1d9a37d8cc9f4a91","cmd-b9bee638e2324bdf","cmd-37a8c8cae3ab439c","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Prefer the in-memory swap over any disk-backed swap.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The recovered zram swap had priority 32767, the maximum Linux swap priority, and it was the only active swap shown.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9bf851a2208c4953","cmd-37a8c8cae3ab439c"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified: configuration in cmd-bec683a148c548da directly implemented the task, and the reboot in cmd-1d9a37d8cc9f4a91 established boot persistence and mandatory restart evidence. The reboot command did leave /tmp/antrieb-reboot.log behind; this small executor-created temporary residue remained after completion and slightly reduces hygiene.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bec683a148c548da","cmd-1d9a37d8cc9f4a91","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. Node1 has 512 MiB of zstd-compressed zram swap at priority 32767, and a verified reboot showed a changed boot identity followed by recovery of the swap and platform services. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete and corroborated by lifecycle boot-identity observations.","limitations":["The lifecycle collector cannot assess failed OpenRC services because its failed-service probe is systemd-specific and reported unsupported; however, executor evidence directly showed the relevant services healthy after reboot.","A small reboot log remained in /tmp after execution."]}
